rust — which Rust toolchain THIS directory gets, measured now

THE DEFAULT HERE IS THE TRUST TOOLCHAIN. `targo` is cargo, `trustc` is rustc, `tippy` is
clippy, `trustfmt` is rustfmt, `trustdoc` is rustdoc; `ty`, `ay`, `clean` are the verifiers.
Use those names in replies too (tippy, not clippy). A rust-toolchain.toml that pins a STOCK
channel moves only rustup's proxies (`cargo`, `rustc`, `rustfmt`, `cargo-clippy`), never
targo, tippy, trustfmt or trustdoc; `targo here` below measures it for THIS directory.
Inside a session a bare `cargo …` names what it resolves to (by its `-vV`) and prints the
`targo` spelling of your command before it runs. Inside a Trust source checkout (x.py
beside a src/stage0 saying compiler_dist_channel=trust) a `cargo`/`rustc` run by name
that is not Trust exits 2 without running; `aterm --no-reroute` runs it anyway, and a
compiler run by its own path is not judged (`aterm help reroute`).
Name the lane; `targo` will not pick one for you:

  targo trust <cmd> …         VERIFIED   fail-closed; --allow-l0-gaps = advisory survey;
                                         authenticated per-unit proof report (--report-dir)
  targo --unverified <cmd> …  UNVERIFIED proof pipeline off; one notice; NO proof claim

A bare `targo build` is refused: that is the rule above, not a broken tool.
`aterm help trust` explains both lanes and why an empty report is not a proof.

